From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: itsdunintime104 <270179414+itsdunintime104@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:54:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Settings: Upscaling is shown with the first rows

MetalFX presenting is the choice that goes with a fullscreen size above the game's picture, so it sits beside Display mode and Fullscreen resolution instead of under Advanced settings. Only the row's level changes: the default stays off.

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: the Upscaling choice belongs beside the Fullscreen resolution it works with, not under Advanced settings
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#929

---
 dm/games/settings.tsv                    | 2 +-
 dm/tools/tests/test_launcher_settings.py | 2 +-
 docs/settings.md                         | 4 ++--
 3 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/games/settings.tsv b/dm/games/settings.tsv
index 87f606a..55abf58 100644
--- a/dm/games/settings.tsv
+++ b/dm/games/settings.tsv
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ DM_PRESENT_INTERVAL	choice	game=30 fps,display=60 fps	display	DM_GAME_PRESENT_DI
 DM_DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION	toggle	-	0	fixups:DYNAMIC_RESOLUTION	Game	Dynamic resolution	Lets the game lower its resolution under load. Turn off to keep full resolution for the selected console mode.
 DM_RENDER_SCALE	range	0.5:1.0:0.05	1.0	fixups:RENDER_SCALE	Game	Render scale		level=basic
 DM_OPMODE	choice	1=Docked,0=Handheld	DM_GAME_OPMODE	always	Game	Console mode		level=basic
-DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE	choice	off=Standard,metalfx=MetalFX	off	always	Game	Upscaling	Uses more GPU time and can increase heat.
+DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE	choice	off=Standard,metalfx=MetalFX	off	always	Game	Upscaling	Uses more GPU time and can increase heat.	level=basic
 DM_UPSCALER	choice	game=Game's own,metalfx=MetalFX	game	DM_GAME_UPSCALER_N!=0	Game	Game's upscaler
 DM_LANG	choice	languages	build:DM_LANG	languages>1	Game	Game language		level=basic
 DM_FULLSCREEN	choice	0=Window,1=Fullscreen	0	platform:mac	Game	Display mode		level=basic
diff --git a/dm/tools/tests/test_launcher_settings.py b/dm/tools/tests/test_launcher_settings.py
index d53d943..540058b 100644
--- a/dm/tools/tests/test_launcher_settings.py
+++ b/dm/tools/tests/test_launcher_settings.py
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@ class LauncherSettingsTests(unittest.TestCase):
             listed = settings.build(BOTW, tmp, Path(tmp) / 'control.nacp')
         rows = {s['env']: s for s in listed['settings']}
         self.assertEqual(listed['schema'], 1)
-        self.assertEqual([e for e, s in rows.items() if s.get('level') == 'basic'], ['DM_FPS_TARGET', 'DM_RENDER_SCALE', 'DM_OPMODE', 'DM_LANG', 'DM_RUMBLE'])
+        self.assertEqual([e for e, s in rows.items() if s.get('level') == 'basic'], ['DM_FPS_TARGET', 'DM_RENDER_SCALE', 'DM_OPMODE', 'DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE', 'DM_LANG', 'DM_RUMBLE'])
         self.assertEqual(rows['DM_RUMBLE_GAIN']['needs'], 'DM_RUMBLE=1')
         self.assertFalse({'level', 'needs'} & set(rows['DM_METAL_HUD']), 'a row without meta has no optional fields')
 
diff --git a/docs/settings.md b/docs/settings.md
index 4e02423..05370d8 100644
--- a/docs/settings.md
+++ b/docs/settings.md
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ Breath of the Wild renders 1280x720 in handheld mode. Docked it renders its worl
 
 - **When to change it:** turn it on if the picture looks soft and the device has GPU time to spare: on a Mac, or on an iPhone in handheld mode at 30 fps. For long sessions at 60 fps on an iPhone leave it at Standard.
 - **Cost:** more GPU time each frame, which can increase heat on an iPhone. [Breath of the Wild's measurements](../dm/games/01007EF00011E000/README.md#upscaling-current) cover Mac and iPhone; the matching iPhone Standard run and MetalFX's share of the thermal cost remain unmeasured. Nothing changes while the game's picture is as large as the screen. Unsupported devices and sizes use Standard scaling.
-- **On the Mac:** choose **MetalFX** under **Upscaling** in the [settings window](#the-mac-settings-window)'s Advanced settings, or set `DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE=metalfx` in its `env.txt` (off by default). It helps in a large window or on a 4K screen.
+- **On the Mac:** choose **MetalFX** under **Upscaling** in the [settings window](#the-mac-settings-window), or set `DM_PRESENT_UPSCALE=metalfx` in its `env.txt` (off by default). It helps in a large window or on a 4K screen.
 
