 ## The Mac settings window
 
-A Mac app ([A Mac app](development.md#a-mac-app)) shows its settings in a window before the game starts. They are the same settings as on the iPhone, with the same defaults. The window shows the most used ones first: **Frame rate**, **Render scale**, **Console mode**, **Game language**, **Display mode**, **Fullscreen resolution** and **Game rumble**, when the game has them. **Render scale** shows the picture's size in pixels beside the percentage for the chosen **Console mode**, when the game's profile has it (Breath of the Wild: 1600 × 900 docked, 1280 × 720 handheld at 100 %). The others are under **Advanced settings**, in the usual sections, with **Reset to tested defaults**. The window remembers whether Advanced settings is open. **Frame-rate counter** and **Touch feedback** are only on the iPhone.
+A Mac app ([A Mac app](development.md#a-mac-app)) shows its settings in a window before the game starts. They are the same settings as on the iPhone, with the same defaults. The window shows the most used ones first: **Frame rate**, **Render scale**, **Console mode**, **Upscaling**, **Game language**, **Display mode**, **Fullscreen resolution** and **Game rumble**, when the game has them. **Render scale** shows the picture's size in pixels beside the percentage for the chosen **Console mode**, when the game's profile has it (Breath of the Wild: 1600 × 900 docked, 1280 × 720 handheld at 100 %). The others are under **Advanced settings**, in the usual sections, with **Reset to tested defaults**. The window remembers whether Advanced settings is open. **Frame-rate counter** and **Touch feedback** are only on the iPhone.
 
 Click **Play** (or press Return) to start the game. **Quit**, ⌘Q or closing the window ends the app without the game. The app remembers your choices for that game, and a game started without the window, from a front end or with the window turned off, uses them too ([Saved choices](frontends.md#saved-choices)). A setting fixed by an `env.txt` or by the program that started the app is shown greyed out.
 
